# raw ClinicalTrials.gov v2 role payloads (content-keyed, refetchable)
.ctgov-raw-cache/
outputs/pubmed_databank_cache/
outputs/pubmed_esearch_cache/

# Regenerated figure exports. ssot/figures.py:243 writes these from the PNG
# raster on every build (PIL, compression=None -- 20 files, 275 MB). They are
# a by-product, not a source: untracked and unignored until now, so they sat
# in every `git status`. Ignoring the TIFFs only; the rest of figs/ (eps, svg,
# png, html, _raster_cache) is still undecided -- see TOOLING-QUEUE.md, which
# asks whether the export set is an artefact or a by-product and says not to
# resolve it by committing the current files.
figs/*.tiff

# figs/ export by-products -- 2026-08-27
# Regenerable by ssot/figures.py on demand and consumed only by the F1000 submission
# path, so nothing is lost by not tracking them. They were untracked AND unignored,
# which made `git status --porcelain` non-empty permanently -- and
# scripts/lane_rob/provenance.py:59 calls that WITHOUT --untracked-files=no, so every
# provenance record the lane wrote carried git_dirty=true because of these files.
# The structural fix (per-topic figure directories instead of one shared mutable name
# across 53 topics) remains open in TOOLING-QUEUE.md; this only stops the by-products
# poisoning the build stamp.
figs/*.eps
figs/*.png
figs/*.tiff
figs/*_src.svg
figs/_raster_cache/
